# The town stabler: one per friendly settlement, standing in the yard
# (MapComponent_TSC_GuildFactor stamps the stable). Sells pack animals for
# silver. Brief by design - he is a service, and the named characters carry
# the writing - but he is the only merchant in town who sells something with
# opinions.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_TownStabler

== start ==
The yard smells of straw and warm animal. A stabler comes out of the back range wiping their hands, takes one look at the packs on your shoulders, and reaches for a halter.

"You're carrying it all yourselves. I can fix that. Silver, and it walks out with you."

* "Show us what you've got." -> end
    do stable_animals()
* "How do they do on the road?" -> road
* "Just resting our feet." -> end

== road ==
"Better than you do, most of them." They scratch something behind the ear without looking at it.

"They eat every day, mind. A beast is a bargain you keep making. Feed them, don't work them lame, and they'll carry what four of you can't." A shrug. "Lose one on the road and that's silver you'll not see again."

* "Let's see them, then." -> end
    do stable_animals()
* "We'll think on it." -> end
